\label{theo:LLL}
        Let $\mathcal{B}$ be a finite family of random events in a probability space $(\Omega, \mathbb{P})$ and let $\sim$ be a dependency relation on $\mathcal{B}$. Suppose that there exist $p \in [0,1)$ and $d \in \mathbb{N}^+$ such that:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item $\mathbb{P}[B] \leqslant p$ and $|\set{B' \in \mathcal{B} \,:\, B' \sim B}| \leqslant d$ for all $B \in \mathcal{B}$,
            \item $\mathsf{e} p d \leqslant 1$, where $\mathsf{e} = 2.718\ldots$ is the base of the natural logarithm. 
        \end{itemize}
        Then $\mathbb{P}\left[\bigcup \mathcal{B}\right] < 1$ and, in particular, $\Omega \setminus \bigcup \mathcal{B} \neq \varnothing$.

